{:receipt :kotobase/surface-collection-reachability
 :date "2026-08-18"
 :for "h7-parse-only-addressable-values"
 :why
 "h7's change is `parse only the collections the request's surface can
  address`, and until now that phrase had no referent. A filter derived from a
  guess is the dangerous version of this hypothesis: a surface that CAN reach a
  collection we filtered out reads `not found` -- a silent wrong answer, and on
  a write it would re-create the document and diverge the graph.

  So the map is read out of the handlers rather than assumed."

 :source "kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocols, src/kotobase/protocols/*.cljc,
          grepped for the collection keys each handler actually passes to
          IStore"

 :map
 {:atproto  #{:kotobase.at/records :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :s3       #{:kotobase.s3/objects :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :git      #{:kotobase.git/objects :kotobase.git/refs :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :pinning  #{:kotobase.protocols/pins :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :blocks   #{:kotobase.protocols/blocks :kotobase.protocols/cid-mismatch
              :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :issues   #{:kotobase.issue/issues :kotobase.issue/proposals
              :kotobase.issue/reviews :kotobase.issue/id-seq
              :kotobase.protocols/audit}
  :sparql   :everything
  :cypher   :everything
  :gremlin  :everything
  :graphql  :everything}

 :the-four-query-surfaces-get-no-filter
 "They query the whole document space by definition, so h7 cannot help them and
  must not try. They are also the four that answer 401 to a self-issued CACAO,
  so they are not the surfaces organic traffic would use."

 :what-the-map-implies-before-any-bench-runs
 {:census-from "test/kotobase_protocols_worker/hydrate_phase_bench.cljs, seed of
                the real production graph"
  :seed-bytes 4930593
  :in-s3-objects 4312242
  :in-git-objects 158281
  :in-the-other-15-collections 460070
  :consequence
  "An atproto request addresses `:kotobase.at/records` and audit. It currently
   parses all 526 s3 objects -- 87.5% of the seed by bytes -- plus the git
   objects, on every request. The s3 collection is not even reachable from this
   graph by an s3 request any more: since 2026-08-10 `graph/for-request` routes
   an s3 request for a bucket to `s3-bucket/<bucket>`, its own chain. Only the
   four credential-gated query surfaces can still reach those documents here."}

 :the-hazard-this-map-exists-to-prevent
 "A filter is a PREDICTION about reachability, and a wrong prediction is silent:
  the read returns nothing rather than failing. Two rules follow --
   1. the map is derived from the handlers, and moves when they move;
   2. an unknown surface filters NOTHING. Fail open on the parse, because the
      failure mode of filtering too little is cost and the failure mode of
      filtering too much is a wrong answer."

 :not-yet-implemented
 "This is the input h7 needs, not h7. Landing order is unchanged: the phase
  bench re-measures h1/h6/h7 first, because their :after-harness values were
  all taken against the old decode2 and are overstated."}
